<title>CHILE: Mexico's Tribasa wins Chile highway bid.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Tribasa wins Chile highway bid.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Mexican building company Tribasa won Monday a concession to upgrade a stretch of the Panamerican highway from Chillan to Collipulli in southern Chile, said the public works ministry.</p>
<p>Tribasa offered the lowest toll, 1,000 pesos per vehicle, to operate the 170 kilometer-long stretch of road for nearly 22 years.</p>
<p>The toll and operating period were lower than those offered in bids from Chilean companies Infrasestructura 2000, headed by power giant Endesa, and Obras Viales.</p>
</text>
